## Per-competitor execution skills

One skill per competitor in `data/competitors.json`. Each drives the competitor against `<uc>` structure + `data-sources/`, then hands raw output to `uc-run--register-competitor-answers`. Each should also emit `stats.json` fields it knows (model, time, tokens, cost) and the `instructions.md` body actually used.

### uc-run--competitor--normain

- drive Normain (own product) against `<uc>`
- emit raw answers + `citedSources` if exposed by the product
- capture model + timing

### uc-run--competitor--claude

- call Claude API w/ `data-sources/` attached (files API or inlined)
- pin model id + system prompt per run
- emit raw answers + token/cost stats

### uc-run--competitor--claude-code

- spawn Claude Code session w/ `data-sources/` mounted as working dir
- feed questions, capture responses
- emit raw answers + model + tokens

### uc-run--competitor--claude-cowork

- drive Claude Cowork flow against `<uc>`
- likely manual paste step
- emit raw answers + capture model/timing

### uc-run--competitor--chatgpt-thinking

- ChatGPT (Thinking mode) — manual paste loop
- capture prompts + responses verbatim into `answerRaw`
- emit raw answers

### uc-run--competitor--m365-copilot

- M365 Copilot — manual run, `data-sources/` uploaded to OneDrive/SharePoint
- record source-exposure setup in `instructions.md`
- emit raw answers

### uc-run--competitor--gemini-dr

- Gemini Deep Research — kick off research task, wait for report
- map report sections → per-question answers
- emit raw answers + time

### uc-run--competitor--notebooklm

- upload `data-sources/` to a NotebookLM notebook
- ask each question, collect responses (+ NotebookLM-cited sources → `citedSources`)
- emit raw answers

